    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for cpupower",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for cpupower fixes the following issue:\n\n- CVE-2026-80663: tools/power/x86/intel-speed-select: Harden daemon pidfile open (bsc#1278335).\n\nChanges for cpupower:\n\n- intel-speed-select: Harden daemon pidfile open (git-fixes, bsc#1278335, CVE-2026-80663)\n- turbostat: Fix microcode patch level output for AMD/Hygon (git-fixes)\n- cpupower: Reset errno before strtoull() (stable-fixes)\n- intel-speed-select: Fix file descriptor leak in isolate_cpus() (git-fixes)\n- cpupower: Fix incorrect size in cpuidle_state_disable() (stable-fixes)\n- cpupower: fix error return value in cpupower_write_sysfs() (stable-fixes)\n- cpufreq: Fix a bug where the -t option of the set subcommand was not working (stable-fixes)\n- turbostat: Clustered Uncore MHz counters should honor show/hide options (stable-fixes)\n- turbostat: Handle non-root legacy-uncore sysfs permissions (stable-fixes)\n- turbostat: Handle cap_get_proc() ENOSYS (stable-fixes)\n- turbostat: Fix build with musl (stable-fixes)\n- cpupower: Fix the snapshot-order of tsc,mperf, clock in mperf_stop() (stable-fixes)\n- power turbostat: Fix bogus SysWatt for forked program (git-fixes)\n- cpupower: bench: Prevent NULL dereference on malloc failure (stable-fixes)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-SL-Micro-6.2-1959",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
